<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92809" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥῠπαίνω</span></b> , fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥῠπᾰνῶ </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταρ-</span>) <i><span class="en">
			Isoc.
			12.63
		</span></i>:—
			Pass.
		, aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρρυπάνθην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.434b
				</span></i>
			: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥύπος</span>):—<i>defile,
				disfigure</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥ. τὸ μακάριον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1099b2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν ἐμὸν βίον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aristaenet.
					2.17
				</span></i>
			; <i>abuse, disparage</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pherecr.
				228
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1405a25
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be</i> or <i>become foul</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαμπρύνεσθαι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Lac.</u>
				11.3
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Apoc.</u>
				22.11
			</span></i>; of a garment, <i>get dirty</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Char.</u>
				10.14
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<i>contaminate, infect</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς πλησιάζοντας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					1.254
				</span></i>
			.</div>
